# pannellum-react (the 360 VR viewer) declares `peer react@16.x`. We're on
# React 19, so npm 7+ refuses to install and the build dies with ERESOLVE.
#
# That declaration is stale metadata, not a real incompatibility. The package
# uses no API React 19 removed — no findDOMNode, no legacy lifecycle methods —
# and it has been running against React 19 locally. It was simply last
# published before React 17 existed and never had its peers updated.
#
# legacy-peer-deps restores npm 6 behaviour: install what the lockfile says and
# warn about peer mismatches instead of failing. Committed rather than passed
# as a CLI flag so Vercel, CI and anyone cloning all resolve identically —
# a flag someone forgets is how "works on my machine" starts.
#
# The real fix is replacing pannellum-react with a maintained viewer. Until
# then this is the honest, contained workaround.
legacy-peer-deps=true
